NAME
     tar - read and write archives

SYNOPSIS
     tar {c|x|t}[v][z]f ARCHIVE [-C DIR] [FILE...]

DESCRIPTION
     tar makes an archive of files, lists one, or unpacks one. It reads
     the ustar and pax formats and writes ustar; with z it uses gzip on
     the way. Unpacking refuses absolute paths and paths with .. in
     them, so an archive cannot write outside the directory it is
     unpacked into.

OPTIONS
     c    create
     x    extract
     t    list
     v    say what it is doing
     z    compressed
     f ARCHIVE   the archive file; - is standard input or output
     -C DIR      change to DIR first

SEE ALSO
     gzip(1), cp(1)
